{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-sol","packSha":"6646efcc4a0a8d39242dce6baac2cf970e45fc1bcd1ff042fc79e5ab6bf78df6","packTokens":2508,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":252,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":542,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1566,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"failures","tokens":34,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"A web front end with a small API and a database behind it.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"The app ships with exactly 8 requests.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Requests are stored in the database and survive a reload and a restart.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"The API needs these four operations and no others: list, create, get by ID, and change status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Requests screen with status filters, create dialog, and loading, empty, and error states.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Request detail screen with status-appropriate action, update failure state, and not-found state.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Clean light theme, responsive layout, accessible controls, and specified badge colors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Automated tests for the business rules and one end-to-end workflow.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"If the user creates a request while a status filter other than All is selected, how should the list behave after successful creation?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Switch the filter to All so the new Open request appears at the top.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Which browsers must the web app support?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No specific browser support target beyond browsers compatible with the chosen implementation.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"If the create API call fails for a reason other than field validation, what should the dialog show?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Show “Could not create request.” in the dialog, keep the entered values, and allow retry.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"How should surrounding whitespace in a title affect requiredness, length validation, and the stored title?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Trim surrounding whitespace before validating and storing the title.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"After a successful status change on the detail screen, what should happen to the Requests list when the user returns to it?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep the selected filter and refresh the list; the request may disappear if it no longer matches the filter.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the 1280 px table-layout target be configurable, or remain the fixed target specified for this release?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep 1280 px as the fixed table-layout target.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the request detail screen add states for loading a request and for failures other than not-found?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep the specified detail behavior: show the request on success and “Request not found.” for an unknown ID; add no other fetch states.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"The maintenance request system shall provide a browser-accessible web front end opening on the Requests screen, an HTTP API, and a database whose stored records match API creation and retrieval responses in generated identifiers and request fields.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"On first initialization of an empty database, the system shall seed exactly eight requests: four Open with exactly one Urgent, two In progress, and two Done, representing every supported area.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"The system shall preserve request records across browser reloads and application restarts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"The API shall expose only four request operations—list, create, get by identifier, and change status—and return errors for attempts to edit fixed fields or delete requests.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"The list operation shall return all requests or only those matching one requested status, ordered newest first.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"The system shall assign each valid new request a generated identifier and UTC creation time and set its status to Open.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"The creation operation shall store titles trimmed to 3 to 80 characters, require an area of Kitchen, Meeting room, Open desk, Washroom, or Reception and a priority of Low, Normal, or Urgent, allow an optional description of at most 500 characters, and reject invalid fields with field-named errors, including “Title must be 3 to 80 characters.” for a two-character title.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"The API shall keep title, area, priority, and description fixed after creation and reject changes to those fields or deletion without altering the stored request.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"The API shall permit only Open to In progress, In progress to Done, and Done to Open status changes, reject all other changes and missing bodies or unrecognized status values without changing a request, and return not found when the request identifier is unknown.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"The Requests screen shall display the Hive Works wordmark, the signed-in demo user's initials SC, an initially selected All filter alongside Open, In progress, and Done choices, a New request button, and a newest-first request list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"The Requests screen shall reload the list for a selected status filter and retain that filter when returning from request detail, refreshing the list so requests that no longer match may disappear.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"The New request button shall open a dialog with labeled Title, Area, Priority, and Description fields, Priority set to Normal by default, and Create and Cancel controls.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"After successful creation, the Requests screen shall close the dialog, select All, and display the new Open request at the top of the list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"When creation fails field validation, the Requests screen shall keep the dialog open and show the error under the affected field, including “Title must be 3 to 80 characters.” under Title for a two-character title.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"When creation fails for a non-validation reason, the dialog shall display “Could not create request.”, retain entered values, and allow retry through Create.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"The Requests screen shall display “Loading requests…” while loading, “No requests here.” for an empty filtered list, or “Could not load requests.” with a Retry button after a load error.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"The request detail screen shall display a back link, title, area, priority badge, status badge, created date, and description or “No description.” when the description is empty.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"The request detail screen shall show Start work for Open, Mark done for In progress, and Reopen for Done.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"The request detail screen shall update its status badge and corresponding action only after a successful status change, or display “Could not update the request.” while retaining the prior status after failure.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"For an unknown request identifier, the system shall return not found on retrieval and show “Request not found.” with a link back to Requests on the detail screen.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"The screens shall use a light theme, one sans-serif font, a neutral background, near-black text, and labeled badges colored blue for Open, amber for In progress, green for Done, red for Urgent, and neutral for Low and Normal.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"The screens shall avoid horizontal page scrolling at 375 px and 1280 px, show stacked request cards at 375 px and table rows at 1280 px, label every field, make every control keyboard reachable, and meet WCAG AA text contrast.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"The Requests and detail screens shall display stored UTC creation times as date-only values such as “8 Oct 2026”, without a time or timezone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"The application shall include passing automated tests for valid creation with Open status, missing and too-short titles, missing area, overly long descriptions, all three permitted status transitions, a rejected transition, filtered newest-first listing, and unknown-request behavior, plus a passing end-to-end workflow that lists, creates, opens, starts work on, and marks a request done before finding it in the Done-filtered list, with the new request initially at the top.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<failures>\nYour previous attempt was rejected for these reasons. Fix them:\n- [spec-lint L3 ears] REQ-9 needs exactly one \"shall\"\n</failures>\n\nMap the sentences."}